  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1146 PM CST Thu Nov 19 2026\n\nA brief break looks to follow for the Panhandles behind the cold\nfront system Sunday with most of the area looking at highs in the\n40s to low 50s. However, this does look to change by late Monday\nas present model agreement continues to see our next system push\nacross the area. At this time, latest ensembles are giving us\naround a 10 to 30 percent chance at precipitation. What make this\ninteresting is that current trends with model have begun to favor\nthis system and its precipitation chances moving in during the\novernight hours. If this timing holds true, then temperatures can\nbe cold enough for some of the Northern Panhandles see their \nfirst snowfall. However, given our current chances of actually \nseeing precipitation, confidence is not too high just yet. \nRegardless this active pattern look to have the opportunity to \ncontinue as models hint at yet another system for the holiday \nitself. Otherwise, temperatures will keep more of that late fall \nfeel to them with highs looking to stay in the 40s through the \nweek.",
